    "ls": {
      "hash": "aba956d096c45f26b4777db24fc612e60c0c480414a9bab945ba1db7a2e54641",
      "text": "[Industry USA] LS ELECTRIC America to Highlight DC Grid Solutions for AI Data Centers at Data Center World 2026 | LS ELECTRIC America Skip to main content Products & Systems Markets Services Support Company search America America Global Korea search open menu America America Global Korea search close menu Products & Systems Markets Services Support Company Explore All Products LS ELECTRIC America to Highlight DC Grid Solutions for AI Data Centers at Data Center World 2026 Apr 03, 2026 LS ELECTRIC America presents direct current (DC) power systems to reduce energy losses and support rising AI workloads at Data Center World 2026. LS ELECTRIC America will highlight its DC grid power system concept for AI data centers at Data Center World 2026, focusing on improving energy efficiency and supporting the rapid growth of high-density AI server infrastructure. Challenge: Rising power demand in AI data centers The increasing use of high-performance AI chips—such as those from NVIDIA—is driving significant growth in server rack power density and thermal loads. LS ELECTRIC will present projections showing how: GPU power consumption is increasing Rack-level power demand is rising through 2028 Cooling and infrastructure requirements are becoming more complex Solution: DC power systems for improved efficiency At the core of LS ELECTRIC’s approach is the use of DC (direct current) power distribution across the data center. Compared with traditional AC systems, DC architectures can: Reduce total power system losses from ~25% to ~10% Minimise energy conversion stages Improve overall electricity utilisation from source to server rack The system integrates technologies such as: Solid State Transformers (SST) DC/DC converters Solid State Circuit Breakers (SSCB) System architecture: From grid to rack The company will demonstrate how DC systems can be applied across the entire energy chain, including: Power generation and grid interface Medium- and low-voltage switchgear UPS and energy storage systems Data hall distribution and rack-level delivery This end-to-end approach supports more efficient and scalable AI data center designs. Cooling strategies: Managing higher heat loads To address increasing thermal demands, LS ELECTRIC will also present various cooling technologies, including: Air-based systems (CRAH, CRAC, cooling towers) Liquid cooling solutions (cold plates, immersion cooling, CDU systems) These solutions are critical for maintaining performance and reliability in high-density AI environments. Industry relevance: Preparing for next-generation AI infrastructure As AI workloads continue to expand, data center operators must rethink both power distribution and cooling strategies. DC grid solutions offer a pathway to: Higher efficiency Reduced operational costs Improved scalability for future AI applications Featured In Read on Industry USA↗ Read on Data Center Technology↗ NEXT LS ELECTRIC Secures $115 Million Power Infrastructure Contract for North American Data Center Growth PREV ESS to Microgrids: Advanced Inverters and Controls for a Resilient Grid LIST Subscribe Newsletter: Efficiency, Delivered Directly. Subscribe to receive real-world case studies, energy-saving tips, and optimized configuration guides tailored for your industry. Email ​ Areas of Interest LV & MV Power Solutions Grid & Utility Infrastructure Automation & Industrial Control Get Insights I agree with the terms of use as described in the Privacy Policy. © 2026 LS ELECTRIC Co., Ltd. All Rights Reserved. LS ELECTRIC Affiliated & Subsidiaries LS ELECTRIC Affiliated & Subsidiaries LS Group LS Cable & System LS MnM LS Mtron Gaon Cable E1 YESCO LS ELECTRIC Global LS Metal LS Mecapion LS Sauter LS Energy Solutions LS e-Mobility Solutions Privacy Policy | Terms of Service | General Terms of Purchase | Change Your Cookie Setting Home Company Articles Articles Articles Contact Us Where to Buy Connect Portal",
