A System DIAEnergie Industrial Energy Management System DIAStudio Smart Machine Suite DIALink Edge Server Box Industrial PC UNOnext Indoor Air Quality Monitor UNOlite Indoor Air Quality Monitor Industrial Lighting Road Lighting Fishing Light Commercial Lighting Indoor Telecom Power System Outdoor Telecom Power System Renewable Hybrid Power System Rectifiers DC/DC Converter Inverters PV Converter Battery Cooling RMMS Uninterruptible Power Supplies Data Center Infrastructure Battery System Photovoltaic Inverter Wind Power Converter DeltaGrid Lighting DeltaGrid Metering DeltaGrid Energy Management Contact Us ESG Download Centre News Center News Blog Event Calendar Delta Brand News About Delta Delta Profile Executives Financials Global Operations Innovation Milestones ESG Careers Home News Center Press Releases 30/9/2026 Delta Electronics Unveils AI Modular Data Center with 800 VDC In-Row Power for NVIDIA Vera Rubin and Microgrid Solutions at Data Center World Asia 2026 Delta Electronics, a global leader in power management and smart green solutions, is attending Data Center World (DCW) Asia 2026 with its new AI Modular Data Center (AI MDC) and Microgrid Solutions to accelerate the deployment and enhance the energy efficiency and resilience of AI infrastructure. The prefabricated AI MDC integrates next-gen 800 VDC In-Row Power and liquid cooling systems for the fast deployment and scalability of AI data centers based on NVIDIA Vera Rubin architecture. The Microgrid Solution integrates Delta’s renewable energy, energy storage, and Solid Oxide Fuel Cell (SOFC) systems, as well as Solid State Transformers (SST), which are essential to directly convert medium voltage power to 800 VDC for the AI factories of the future. “AI workloads are scaling faster than most data centres were designed to handle, while their demands can be increasingly unpredictable. This means infrastructure planning must move from reactive to integrated and future-ready,” said Jason Yuan, President, Southeast Asia & ANZ, Delta Electronics. “Our AI Modular Data Centers and Microgrids, both part of our Grid to-Chip Solutions portfolio, are ideal to help our clients across Southeast Asia deploy and power their future-ready AI data centers. Moreover, Delta’s solutions are engineered for energy efficiency, reliability and performance, while providing the flexibility to adapt to changing workloads and infrastructure demands.” Visitors can expect interactive showcases spanning Delta Electronics’ AI infrastructure portfolio, including its AI Modular Data Center designed for scalability, flexibility, and compatibility, high-voltage direct current (HVDC) 3.6MW in-row coolant distribution unit (CDU) technology to help manage the thermal demands of high-density AI workloads. The showcased 800 VDC In-Row Power architecture features 660kW output power, up to 98% AC-DC efficiency, 480kW capacity in battery backup units (BBU), and aluminium capacitors to optimize GPU workloads in next-generation AI data centres. In addition, Delta’s prefabricated AI Containerized Data Center (CDC) Solutions deliver up to 60 kW per rack of AI compute within the footprint of a single parking space, as well as a seamlessly integrated Liquid-to-Air CDU system to achieve a PUE as low as 1.19. The unveiled Microgrid Solution demonstrates how on-site energy generation resources, energy storage, power conversion, and the new solid state transformer (SST) can support greater power resilience, efficiency and flexibility. Through real time coordination of multiple energy sources, uptime and power quality are maintained during grid connection delays or off-grid operation, with SOFC providing reliable on-site power 24/7. Its prefabricated DC coupled architecture combines SSTs, DC/DC converters and dynamic energy support to reduce conversion stages, enabling the system to respond to fluctuating AI loads while supporting scalable deployment. At the board-level, Delta’s thermal management solutions include a dedicated state-of-the art cold plate for NVIDIA Vera Rubin NVL72, with the latest microchannel and multi impinging flow design. See the Future of AI Infrastructure Live at DCW Asia 2026 Delta Electronics will showcase the In-Row Power at DCW Asia 2026, taking place from 29 30 September at the Marina Bay Sands Convention Centre, Level 1, Singapore, at Booth D10. Sakda Sae-Ueng, SEA & Oceania Data Center Business Platform Head, will also be headlining the Data Centre World Keynote Theatre at 10:25am on Day 1, where he will discuss Delta Electronics’ collaboration with NVIDIA and the roadmap for 800VDC power architecture. Singapore and the Southeast Asia region are increasingly viewed as a regional hub for next generation AI infrastructure, with operators across the region under pressure to deploy at a pace and density that did not exist a cycle ago. Delta Electronics helps customers respond to this shift with integrated power, cooling and energy infrastructure engineered to support the rapid evolution of AI workloads, while providing the flexibility, efficiency and resilience needed to remain future-ready and accelerate the transition towards more sustainable data centers. News Source: Back Related News 5/10/2026 Delta Shares Industry Insights on Malaysia’s Next Phase of Infrastructure Growth at Data Centre Nexus 2026 2/9/2026 Delta Electronics and Singapore Polytechnic Partner to Develop Future Technical Talents 25/8/2026 Delta Electronics Spotlights AI and Integrated Solutions to Advance Semiconductor Packaging at SEMICON Southeast Asia 2026 25/8/2026 Delta Electronics and ITE Collaborate to Build Singapore’s HVDC Capabilities for Next-Generation Infrastructure To provide innovative, clean and energy-efficient solutions for a better tomorrow. Contact Us Regions Language Global - English Global - 繁體中文 Americas - English Australia - English China - 简体中文 EMEA - English EMEA - Deutsch EMEA - Français EMEA - Italiano India - English Japan - 日本語 Korea - 한국어 Singapore - Engl