      "text": "SGC Energy Partners With Vertiv on Gunsan AI Data Center - Seoul Economic Daily Skip to main content Seoul Economic Daily Markets Property Finance Business Technology Politics Society Culture Sports International Opinion AI KEY Seoul Economic Daily KST Seoul Economic Daily Korea's Leading Business News Since 1960 한국어 Markets Property Finance Business Technology Politics Society Culture Sports International Opinion AI KEY Menu Saved Articles Newsletters AI KEY Settings SGC Energy Partners With Vertiv on Gunsan AI Data Center Companies to Cooperate on Maximizing Power and Cooling Efficiency Vertiv's Integrated Power Solution to Debut in South Korea Finance | Published 2026.09.08. 14:27:06 | By Song Ju-hee ssong@sedaily.com | Summary | Save A A A Hwang Se-hoon (right), executive director at SGC Energy, and Jordan Ko, senior director of Asia enterprise sales and emerging markets at Vertiv, pose for a photo after signing a memorandum of understanding on the AI data center business at SGC Group headquarters in Seocho-gu on Nov. 18. /Courtesy of SGC Energy SGC Energy (005090) said on the 8th that it signed a memorandum of understanding with U.S. digital infrastructure company Vertiv Holdings on an artificial intelligence data center project, at the SGC Group headquarters in Seoul's Seocho district on the 18th of last month. Under the agreement, the two companies will jointly conduct technical reviews of the infrastructure for the AI data center SGC Energy is developing in Gunsan and cooperate on adopting solutions that maximize power and cooling efficiency. SGC Energy's AI data center will be built on a modular architecture, and Vertiv plans to deploy its integrated power solution, PowerNexus, for the first time in South Korea. PowerNexus is a prefabricated system that combines core power infrastructure — including uninterruptible power supplies and power distribution equipment — into a single pre-assembled unit. The two companies are jointly designing AI infrastructure for an initial 60-megawatt phase and plan to continue working together as the project expands to as much as 300 megawatts. \"We plan to accelerate the construction of an unrivaled AI data center based on the close partnership between SGC Energy and Vertiv,\" said Hwang Se-hoon, an executive director at SGC Energy. \"Because the AI data center business is a new growth pillar for the company, we will do everything possible to push the project forward without setbacks.\" Jordan Ko, senior director for Asia emerging markets at Vertiv, said the partnership will help develop infrastructure that can support both SGC Energy's current requirements and its future scalability. # SGCEnergy # Vertiv # AIDataCenter # Gunsan # PowerNexus # DataCenter Original reporting by Song Ju-hee for Seoul Economic Daily. AI-translated from Korean. Quotes from foreign sources are based on Korean-language reports and may not reflect exact original wording. View Korean original ↗ Translation Policy Watch · Seoul Economic Daily More → 4:39 NIKE IS OUT After 18 years - Off the Charts 4:39 Related Articles Doosan Enerbility Ships First Gas Turbine to U.S. for SpaceXAI Published 2026.10.06. 14:09:47 Reflection AI, Shinsegae Partner as U.S. Firm Targets China With Low-Cost Model Published 2026.10.06. 11:27:59 Security Stocks Surge After AI Hacking Hits Financial Firms Published 2026.10.06. 17:54:17 Most Read This Week 1 - 5 ‹ › 1 AMRO Lifts Korea's 2026 Growth Forecast Again to 3.3% 2 U.S. Private Colleges Slash Tuition as Applicants Walk Away 3 China's TCL Passes Samsung in LCD TVs, Leads by 0.1 Point 4 42dot Hires Three Global Tech Leaders to Boost SDV Capabilities 5 CJ CheilJedang, ADM Form Feed Amino Acid Joint Venture ← Back to Home ◆ SIGNAL English Edition Read this story 12 hours earlier. Korean capital markets, translated. Subscribers see deals before the wires. Read SIGNAL → Free to browse · 50% intro rate Opinions › Min Byoung-kwon (Commentary) Space Reactors Return as U.S., Ch